##### Git:- distributed version control system,used to track changes in file or espically source code.
>>	 we use git for keep track , maintain history of changes, improve collaboration among the teammates working on same projects. 

### stages of git :-
			1) working directory :- this is where you create or modify files.
			2) staging area :- you select the changes that you want to commit.
			3) local repository :- you permanently save the staged changes in Git's local history.
			4) remote repository :- you send your local commits to a remote repository such as (GitHub,bitbucket,azure repo,gitlab).

>>		 note :- changes moves from working directory-->>staging area-->>local repository-->>remote repository


#### basic commands of Git ####

##  Git Configuration ##
>> check git version :-git --version
>> set username or email :- for username :-git config --global user.name "Akash"
			> :- for email :- git config --global user.email "you@example.com"
 >view git configuration :- git config --list

## Create / Download Repository ##
 >initialize a new Git repository :- git init
 >download/clone an existing repository :- git clone <repository-url>

## Check Repository Status ##
 >check repository :- git status

## add file ##
 >add one file :- git add filename
 >add all changed files in staging :- git add .

## Commit ##
>> Save staged changes into Git history :- git commit -m "Add login feature"
>> view commit history :- git log
>> View compact commit history :- git log --oneline

## branch command ##
 >>list branch :- git branch 
 >>create a branch :- git branch feature-login
 >>switch to branch :- git switch feature-login
 >>switch or create branch :- git switch -c feature-login

## merge ##
> First switch to the branch you want to merge into:
      git switch main
      git merge feature-login

## remote repository ##
 >Show connected remote repositorie :- git remote -v
 >Connect local repository to a remote repository :- git remote add origin <repository-url>

## push ##
 >Push local main branch to remote :- git push origin main
 >first push :- git push -u origin main

## pull and fetch ##
 >Downloads changes and merges them into your current branch :- git pull
 >Downloads remote changes but does not merge them :- git fetch

## view changes ##
 >see unstaged change :- git diff
 >see staged change :- git diff --staged

## undo changes ##
 >discard changes in file :- git restore filename
 >unstage a file :- git restore --staged filename

## Git reset ##
 >Undo the latest commit while keeping the changes in your working directory :- git reset HEAD~1
 >Undo the latest commit and remove its changes :- git reset --hard HEAD~1

## stash ##
 >Temporarily save unfinished changes :- git stash
 >See stashed changes :- git stash list
 >Restore latest stash :- git stash pop

## GitHub ##
> GitHub is a cloud-based platform where we can store and manage Git repositories.
> Git = Tool for version control
> GitHub = Online platform for hosting Git repositories

## use of GitHub ##
> GitHub is used to store, manage, and share code online using Git repositories.
> It helps developers collaborate, track changes, review code, and automate deployments.

## workflow of GitHub ##

> To edit exesting file 

create a branch (git checkout -b branch name)
		|
git pull (latest pull)
		|		
edit changes (code .)
		|
git status(check what changes)
		|
git add (add the change file)
		|
git commit -m "list what you changed" (commit)
		|
git push origin (push your branch)
		|
merge into main ( feature branch -->> push-->> create pull req.-->> merge pull request)



			 
